<article class="env-lemma" id="07HP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07HP">Lemma <span data-tag="07HP">60.5.6</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/07MD" data-tag="07MD">60.5.1</a>. Let $P$ be a polynomial algebra over $A$ and let $P \to C$ be a surjection of $A$-algebras with kernel $J$. With $(D_ e, \bar J_ e, \bar\gamma )$ as in Lemma <a href="/tag/07KG" data-tag="07KG">60.5.5</a>: for every object $(B, J_ B, \delta )$ of $\text{CRIS}(C/A)$ there exists an $e$ and a morphism $D_ e \to B$ of $\text{CRIS}(C/A)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We can find an $A$-algebra homomorphism $P \to B$ lifting the map $C \to B/J_ B$. By our definition of $\text{CRIS}(C/A)$ we see that $p^ eB = 0$ for some $e$ hence $P \to B$ factors as $P \to P_ e \to B$. By the universal property of the divided power envelope we conclude that $P_ e \to B$ factors through $D_ e$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>